See {{:../../doc/awskit.html}[awskit]} for the project overview.

{0 awskit-s3}

Amazon S3 client — objects, buckets, multipart uploads, presigned URLs,
policies, and an in-memory simulation. Parameterized by
{!module-type:Awskit.Runtime.S}.

This package builds on {{:../awskit/index.html}[awskit]}, which provides the
Runtime abstraction, adapters, and signing. The S3 API surface is split into
{b pure types} (this library) and {b runtime-wired operations} (adapter
libraries that actually make HTTP calls).

{1 Libraries}

{2 Library awskit-s3}

The entry point is {!module:Awskit_s3}.

Pure S3 types and operations — no IO dependencies. Use the
{!module:Awskit_s3.Make} functor to create a client with any runtime adapter, or
use one of the pre-built adapter libraries below.

Modules:
{ul
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Credentials} — AWS credentials, re-exported for convenience}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Endpoint} — endpoint configuration, re-exported for convenience}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Object} — get, put, delete, copy, list, head, tagging}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Bucket} — create, delete, list, head, policy,
    versioning, encryption, tagging}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Multipart} — create, upload_part, complete, abort,
    list_parts}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Presigned} — presigned GET and PUT URLs}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Policy} — bucket policy types, JSON round-tripping,
    access evaluation}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Sim} — deterministic in-memory S3 for testing}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Error} — S3-specific error types}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Storage_class} — storage tiers (Standard, Glacier, etc.)}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Range} — byte ranges for partial reads}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Metadata} — custom [x-amz-meta-*] headers}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Tag} — key-value tags on objects and buckets}
}

{2 Library awskit-s3.eio}

The entry point is {!module:Awskit_s3_eio}.

Includes [Awskit_s3.Make(Awskit_eio.Runtime)] — direct-style, no promises.
You can create connections directly from {!module:Awskit_s3_eio}:

{[
open Eio.Std

let () =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  let conn = Awskit_s3_eio.create
    ~env ~region:"us-east-1" ~credentials ()
  in
  let result = Awskit_s3_eio.Object.put conn
    ~bucket:"my-bucket" ~key:"hello.txt" "Hello, S3!"
  in
  match result with
  | Ok { Awskit_s3.Object.Put_result.etag } -> Fmt.pr "Uploaded! ETag: %s" etag
  | Error err -> Fmt.epr "Error: %a" Awskit_s3.Error.pp err
]}

{2 Library awskit-s3.lwt}

The entry point is {!module:Awskit_s3_lwt}.

Generic Lwt adapter layer. Use {!module:Awskit_s3_lwt.Make} to compose
{!module:Awskit_s3} with any [Cohttp_lwt.S.Client] implementation:

{[
module S3 = Awskit_s3_lwt.Make (Cohttp_lwt_unix.Client)

let conn = S3.create
  ~region:"us-east-1"
  ~credentials
  ~clock:Ptime_clock.now
  ()
]}

{2 Library awskit-s3.lwt_unix}

The entry point is {!module:Awskit_s3_lwt_unix}.

Ready-to-use Lwt + Unix adapter. Includes
[Awskit_s3_lwt.Make(Cohttp_lwt_unix.Client)] and provides a default OS clock:

{[
let conn = Awskit_s3_lwt_unix.create
  ~region:"us-east-1" ~credentials ()
|> Result.get_ok
in
let* result = Awskit_s3_lwt_unix.Object.get conn
  ~bucket:"my-bucket" ~key:"hello.txt" ()
in
match result with
| Ok _ -> Lwt.return_unit
| Error err -> Fmt.epr "Error: %a" Awskit_s3.Error.pp err; Lwt.return_unit
]}

[awskit-s3.lwt_unix] delegates standard AWS environment variable reads to
[awskit.unix]. It reads [AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID], [AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY], optional
[AWS_SESSION_TOKEN], [AWS_REGION], and [AWS_DEFAULT_REGION] when corresponding
arguments are omitted.

{1 Quick start with awskit-s3.eio}

{[
open Eio.Std

let () =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  let credentials = Awskit_s3.Credentials.make
    ~access_key_id:"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE"
    ~secret_access_key:"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY"
    ()
  in
  let conn = Awskit_s3_eio.create
    ~env ~region:"us-east-1" ~credentials ()
  in
  let result = Awskit_s3_eio.Object.put conn
    ~bucket:"my-bucket" ~key:"hello.txt" "Hello, S3!"
  in
  match result with
  | Ok { Awskit_s3.Object.Put_result.etag } ->
    Fmt.pr "Uploaded! ETag: %s" etag
  | Error err ->
    Fmt.epr "Error: %a" Awskit_s3.Error.pp err
]}

